Overview

Bring your enthusiasm and talents to Esri, creating&nbsp;industry leading&nbsp;ArcGIS products. The ArcGIS Maps SDKs allow developers to build modern mapping applications for mobile and desktop platforms, with 2D and 3D data&nbsp;visualisation, and online or offline access. This is a fantastic opportunity to join the product development team and support the delivery of regular, high-quality releases in a collaborative and dynamic environment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Help us improve our cross-platform GIS software libraries, built on the latest compilers and C++ standards, and create sample apps, developer documentation, and developer outreach.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Esri has a Relocation Assistance Program and can provide support with relocating to the Cardiff area for this position. Check out more details of the Esri R&amp;D Center - Cardiff!

Responsibilities

• Apply curious, independent thought, and attention to detail to explore and understand the challenges that ArcGIS users face and provide usable, informative feedback on user experience

• Understand the customer, who are software developers, gathering requirements and use cases that translate into actionable code and doc improvements&nbsp;

• Build rich and varied GIS datasets and maps, sample applications and articles that can be used to highlight product capabilities, explain&nbsp;APIs&nbsp;and guide user (developer) practices

• Work with your development team, and teams across Esri, to design, create, and&nbsp;validate&nbsp;the newest datasets and GIS workflows to support field mapping, data collection, spatial analysis and verify the functionality meets us
